# ACT ONE: THE STING

= A murder shatters the peace of the hive. Detective Buzzaria Honeydew is called to investigate.

.PROLOGUE [[purple]] #0# [[storyline Main Mystery]]

= Hive city establishment.

!!WIDE SHOT OF THE HIVE CITY 

!!THE HIVE AT NIGHT — BILLIONS OF LIGHTS

= The murder.

Under the moonlight, the hive glows like a living constellation. Guard bees patrol the perimeter. The rhythm of the colony never stops.

!!TIGHT ON A SHADOW

Moving through a service passage. Unseen. Unauthorized.

!!QUICK CUTS:

- A comb door opens silently.
- A figure in a hooded cloak moves through the dark.
- The royal chamber, lit by moonbeams.
- Wilfred Wingsby, asleep at his desk.

The shadow approaches. A stinger gleams.

WILFRED
(startling awake)
Who — !

A single strike. Precise.

The shadow flees.

Wilfred collapses. His wings quiver. Then still.

>SILENCE. THE HIVE SLEEPS. A MURDER HAS OCCURRED.<

!!FADE TO BLACK


!!WIDE SHOT OF THE HIVE CITY — DAWN

The great hive hums with activity. Thousands of bees move in geometric patterns, a civilization suspended in golden light. The hexagonal comb stretches endlessly, lit by warm amber glow.

Worker bees depart and return. The rhythm of the hive is hypnotic. Pollen is sorted. Nectar is processed. The economy of the colony flows like a single organism.

>THE HIVE CITY - A MASTERPIECE OF NATURE AND INDUSTRY<

Beneath the surface order, there is tension. The drone population has grown restless. Rumors of reform whisper through the corridors.

Somewhere deep inside, a scream is silenced.

!!SLOW ZOOM TOWARD THE ROYAL CHAMBER


INT. ROYAL CHAMBER - DAWN [[red]] #1#

= Hive patrol finds the body

The body of WILFRED WINGSBY lies crumpled against a honeycomb wall. His wings are torn at unnatural angles. A single sting puncture marks his thorax — precise, clinical. This was no accident.

[[marker red: Document all wound characteristics before autopsy]]

SIR BUZZALOT (V.O.)
(whispering into radio)
We have a situation in the royal wing.
(brief pause)
Code Gold. Repeat, Code Gold. All units lockdown sector seven.

SIR BUZZALOT, head of hive security — a stout bee with battle-scarred wings and a permanent look of concern — stands over the body. His antennae twitch with agitation. He has seen death before. Never this close to the throne.

The chamber is pristine. No signs of struggle. The royal comb glows faintly in the dawn light.

SIR BUZZALOT
(to arriving guard)
Seal the chamber. No one enters. The Detective will want to see it exactly as we found it.

GUARD
Sir, yes sir!

The guard scrambles to obey. Yellow silk caution tape is strung across the entrance.

!!CLOSE ON THE VICTIM'S FACE — PEACEFUL, SURPRISED

SIR BUZZALOT
(muttering)
Who would do this? Inside the royal chamber...

He looks around. The security of the chamber should have been impregnable.

SIR BUZZALOT
(calling out)
Where is the night watch?

A nervous worker bee steps forward, trembling.

NIGHT WATCH
(stammering)
I-I didn't see anything, Sir. I swear! The corridor was empty all night.

SIR BUZZALOT
(skeptical)
Empty? Then how did a murderer —

He stops himself. This isn't the time for blame.

SIR BUZZALOT
(sighing)
Wait for the Detective.


INT. DETECTIVE'S OFFICE - MORNING [[blue]] #2#

= Detective Buzzaria Honeydew is introduced at her office and gets a call about the murder.

BUZZARIA HONEYDEW — our detective. Sharp eyes. Worn wings with tiny battle-nicks. A badge made of polished propolis pinned to her thorax. She sips nectar from a thimble-sized cup — her third this morning.

Her office is a testament to a life of investigation: cold case files pinned to honeycomb walls. Photographs of unsolved mysteries. A map of the hive marked with pushpins in various colors.

She examines a tiny magnifying glass, her most trusted tool. It has solved more cases than any partner.

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
Another day. Another drop of honey.

The light through the window catches a framed photo on her desk. A younger Buzzaria, smiling, next to a bee with familiar features. She glances at it, then away.

!!CLOSE ON THE PHOTO — A MEMORY

The phone buzzes. She picks it up with her forelegs.

SIR BUZZALOT (V.O.)
(urgent)
Buzz, we need you at the royal chamber.
(beat)
Now.

BUZZARIA
(under her breath)
Always when I'm off duty.

She grabs her coat — a tiny leaf stitched into a trench coat style. She slides her magnifying glass into a pocket.

BUZZARIA
(calling out)
I'm heading out! Hold my calls!

She pauses at the door. Looks at the cold case wall.

BUZZARIA
(softer)
One more for the wall, or one more solved?

She doesn't wait for an answer.

!!CLOSE UP ON THE BADGE — HIVE INVESTIGATIONS

>DETECTIVE BUZZARIA HONEYDEW - HIVE INVESTIGATIONS<


!!EXTREME WIDE SHOT OF THE HIVE INTERIOR [[color green]]

Buzzaria navigates the hive's vertical cityscape. The scale is staggering — twelve levels of comb, each with its own ecosystem of activity. [[marker green: Emphasize scale of the hive — this is a civilization]]

Bees of all castes zip past:
- Workers carrying golden pollen loads
- Drones loitering near the mating chamber
- Guards patrolling in precise formations
- Nurse bees tending to larvae in the nursery level

The hive is alive with purpose. Every bee has a role. Every role matters.

A YOUNG WORKER nearly collides with her.

YOUNG WORKER
(sorry)
Oh! Sorry, ma'am! Didn't see you!

BUZZARIA
(smiling)
Watch where you're flying, kid. We don't need two casualties today.

The worker gulps and zips away.

Buzzaria flies past the nursery level. Hundreds of larval cells, each containing a developing bee. Nurse bees feed them royal jelly.

She pauses. Watches.

BUZZARIA
(musing)
Born into a role. No choice in who you become.
(a beat)
Unless you make the choice.

She resumes course, heading upward. Toward the royal chamber.

[[marker orange: Add more establishing shots of the hive here]]


INT. ROYAL CHAMBER - DAY [[purple]] #3# [[storyline Main Investigation, Pollen Trail]]

= Buzzaria arrives at the crime scene, analyzes clues with Honeysuckle, and finds lavender pollen.

Buzzaria ducks under the yellow caution tape — spun silk, marked with "DO NOT CROSS" in hexagonal script. The weight of the crime scene settles on her.

HONEYSUCKLE, the crime scene analyst, a meticulous bee in sterile white gear, circles the body like a vulture examining carrion. Her movements are precise, surgical.

HONEYSUCKLE
(professional, without looking up)
Single sting wound. Precise. Entry angle suggests... another bee.
(gesturing with a tweezer)
The trajectory enters at forty-seven degrees. That's a practiced strike, not a wild swing.

BUZZARIA
(studying the body, not touching)
Could it be a rogue wasp? We've had incursions from the eastern field.

HONEYSUCKLE
(shaking head firmly)
No. Wasps leave a different toxin signature. Their venom is alkaline.
(holding up a test strip)
This is acidic. Bee venom. Pure strain.
(pause)
This was one of us.

BUZZARIA
(leaning in, bold)
Show me the entry point.

HONEYSUCKLE uses a tiny light to illuminate the wound. Buzzaria examines it closely through her magnifying glass.

BUZZARIA
(noticing)
There's a second puncture. Shallower.

HONEYSUCKLE
(surprised)
I — I almost missed that. It's under the main wound.

BUZZARIA
(slowly)
Two strikes. The first one -- hesitant. The second -- decisive.
(evaluating)
This wasn't a professional killer.
(beat)
This was someone who hesitated.

HONEYSUCKLE
(impressed)
That's... remarkably insightful.

BUZZARIA
(wryly)
Twenty years of looking at dead bodies. You learn to listen.

She notices a faint yellow powder on the victim's wing. She gently touches it, smells it.

BUZZARIA
(nose working)
Pollen. Unusual for the royal chamber. Most pollen is filtered before it reaches this level.

[[marker orange: Check pollen type for source identification — CRITICAL CLUE]]

She sniffs again. Closes her eyes.

BUZZARIA
Identification: Lavender. The field on the east side. About half a mile from the hive.

HONEYSUCKLE
(bewildered)
You can tell that just by smell? I'd need a spectral analysis for that kind of precision.

BUZZARIA
(opening eyes, small smile)
When you've been doing this as long as I have, you learn that a nose is faster than any machine.

She looks around the chamber. Something is off.

BUZZARIA
The comb here. Clean. Too clean. Where are his personal effects?

SIR BUZZALOT
(entering)
We... we moved them. Evidence protocol.

BUZZARIA
(turning sharply)
Show me. Everything.




INT. MORGUE - DAY [[green]] #4#

= Dr. Stingson performs the autopsy and discovers royal jelly traces in the wound.

A sterile chamber in the lower levels. Dimly lit. The cold of the outer wall seeps in. The body lies on a slab of polished beeswax, cleaned of surface evidence.

DR. STINGSON, the medical examiner, is a bespectacled bee with a perpetual grimace and a dry sense of humor. He adjusts his headlamp, the light gleaming off his bald head.

DR. STINGSON
(narrating as he works, matter-of-fact)
Time of death: approximately four hours before discovery. The sting entered through the dorsal plate, severing the primary nerve cluster.
(gesturing)
Death would have been — not instant. But swift. Seconds.
(pause)
He didn't suffer long.

BUZZARIA
(businesslike)
Signs of struggle? Defensive wounds?

DR. STINGSON
(holding up a wing fragment)
Minor. Some chips on the wing edge. But nothing that suggests a prolonged fight.
(beat)
He was taken by surprise. Or he trusted the killer.

That detail hits Buzzaria. Trust. That makes this personal.

BUZZARIA
(quiet)
Anything unusual in the toxin?

DR. STINGSON
(pulling out a slide)
Now that you mention it... there was a trace component. Not venom.
(peering through his microscope)
A compound usually found in royal jelly.

BUZZARIA
(eyes narrowing)
Royal jelly?

DR. STINGSON
(nodding)
Traces on the stinger itself. As if the killer had handled royal comb shortly before the attack.

He uses a tiny tweezer to extract something glinting from the wound.

DR. STINGSON
This was lodged in the wound channel.

He holds up a microscopic fragment — a sliver of comb, golden and unmistakable.

BUZZARIA
(taking it carefully)
That's from the Queen's reserve. The royal comb. Only accessible from the throne room's private stores.

DR. STINGSON
(removing glasses, grave)
Someone has access to the highest levels of the hive. And that someone is dangerous.

[[marker red: CRUCIAL CLUE — royal jelly fragment embedded in wound]]

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
The Queen's reserve. The royal chamber. The trust of a victim who let his guard down.
(eyes hardening)
This is an inside job.


INT. THRONE ROOM - DAY [[orange]] #5# [[storyline Main Investigation, Political Subplot]]

= Buzzaria interviews Queen Aster and learns of political conflict with the drone caucus.

A vast chamber that takes Buzzaria's breath away, even after all these years. The ceiling arches fifty feet above. QUEEN ASTER sits on a throne of sculpted comb, her abdomen gleaming with regal stripes of gold and black. She is magnificent — and terrifying in her stillness.

Her court surrounds her. Attendants, advisors, guards. The power of the hive radiates from her.

QUEEN ASTER
(calm, measured)
Detective. I was told you would come.

Her voice is honeyed and commanding. She has ruled for five seasons. She has seen conspiracies before.

BUZZARIA
(bowing respectfully, but not subservient)
Your Majesty. I need to ask you some questions about Wilfred Wingsby.

QUEEN ASTER
(a flicker of something — grief? — passes over her face)
Wilfred served me for twelve seasons. He was my most trusted advisor.
(composing herself)
He was loyal. Brilliant. And now he is... gone.

BUZZARIA
(notebook ready, gently)
Did he have enemies, Your Majesty?

QUEEN ASTER
(a long pause)
In a hive of sixty thousand, Detective, everyone has enemies.
(a subtle emphasis)
Even I have enemies.

BUZZARIA
(pressing, careful)
Specifically, ma'am. Anyone who might want him dead.

QUEEN ASTER
(sighing, the weight of command evident)
Wilfred was... involved in the budget hearings. The drones were furious about the nectar rationing. He advocated for the workers, for stockpiling against the winter.
(leaning forward, significantly)
The drone caucus wanted immediate spending on expansion. Wilfred blocked them.

BUZZARIA
(scribbling in her tiny notebook)
The drone caucus. Led by Dax Droneworth.

QUEEN ASTER
(her expression darkening)
You know of him.

BUZZARIA
I've heard the name. He has ambitions.

QUEEN ASTER
(softly, dangerously)
We all have ambitions, Detective. The difference is what we're willing to do to achieve them.

She holds Buzzaria's gaze. There is a warning there.

QUEEN ASTER
Speak to Dax. But be careful.
(leaning back)
He is not a bee who takes scrutiny well.

[[marker orange: Check Dax Droneworth's alibi — budget meeting or not?]]

!!CLOSE UP ON THE QUEEN'S FACE — HIDDEN DEPTHS




INT. POLITICAL WING - DAY [[yellow]] #6#

= Buzzaria questions Dax Droneworth who provides a strong alibi and criticizes the victim.

The drone wing of the hive. It's louder here. More assertive. Drones buzz with self-importance.

DAX DRONEWORTH is a large, imposing drone with perfectly groomed antennae and a pin-striped thorax. He stands behind a desk made of rare honeycomb — the kind reserved for royalty.

DAX
(defensive, before she even sits)
I was in a budget meeting all night. Dozens of witnesses.
(ticking off points)
The night manager. Three aides. Two internal auditors.
(spreading his forelegs)
I have the cleanest alibi in the hive.

BUZZARIA
(flat, unimpressed)
No one said you didn't, Mister Droneworth.

She sits. Takes out her notebook. Slowly. Letting the silence do its work.

DAX
(uncomfortable with the silence)
I know how this works. The Queen's favorite advisor gets murdered, and you look at the person who disagreed with him.
(scoffs)
Politics doesn't mean murder. It means disagreement. There's a difference.

BUZZARIA
(calm)
What was your last conversation with Wilfred Wingsby?

DAX
(a flicker of hesitation — barely perceptible)
We discussed the budget. The nectar reserve allocation. He was being unreasonable.
(waving a leg dismissively)
He wanted to stockpile eighty percent of the spring harvest. That's insane. We need to expand. Build new comb. Strengthen the hive.

BUZZARIA
(pressing)
And when he refused?

DAX
(hardening)
I told him he was making a mistake. That the drone caucus would remember his obstruction.

BUZZARIA
(leaning forward)
Was that a threat, Mister Droneworth?

DAX
(too quickly, flustered)
It was a prediction. Political prediction. There's a difference.
(composing himself)
I am a politician, Detective. I threaten people's careers, not their lives.

BUZZARIA
(standing, smoothly)
I'll be in touch if I have more questions.

She pauses at the door.

BUZZARIA
(over her shoulder)
Nice comb, by the way. The royal pattern. That must have cost a pretty pollen.

Dax's face falls. He knows what she's implying.

[[marker yellow: Check Dax's access to royal comb stores]]


INT. FUNERAL CHAMBER - DAY [[purple]] #7A#

= The hive attends Wilfred's funeral where Buzzaria notices Pippa Pollen's emotional reaction.

The hive grieves.

A vast chamber filled with honeycomb. At the center, Wilfred Wingsby's body lies in state on a slab of white wax. Flowers — lavender, rose, wildflower — surround him.

Hundreds of bees file past. Some weep. Others bow their heads in silent respect.

QUEEN ASTER stands at the head of the procession. Her expression is unreadable — a mask of royal composure. But those who look closely see her antennae tremble.

QUEEN ASTER
(addressing the gathered hive, voice echoing)
Wilfred Wingsby served this hive for twelve seasons.
(scanning the crowd)
He was a mentor. A leader. A friend.
(her voice catches briefly)
He believed in a hive where every bee mattered. Where truth was more important than politics.

She pauses. Collects herself.

QUEEN ASTER
(continuing, stronger)
His death leaves a wound in our heart. But we must not let fear divide us.
(meeting eyes across the room)
We must honor his memory by seeking the truth. By holding accountable whoever did this.

The crowd buzzes in agreement.

BUZZARIA stands at the back of the chamber. She watches the Queen. She watches the mourners.

She notices PIPPA POLLEN at the far edge of the crowd. The secretary's face is streaked with tears. But there's something else in her expression — something complicated.

!!CLOSE ON PIPPA — GRIEF... OR GUILT?

BUZZARIA
(to herself, observing)
The guilty often return to the scene.
(pause)
Or to the funeral.

One by one, the bees pay their respects. The hive mourns in silence.


INT. FUNERAL RECEPTION - DAY [[pink]]

= Buzzaria notices fresh lavender at the reception and decides to follow the trail.

After the ceremony. Bees gather in an adjoining chamber. Subdued conversation. Nectar is served in tiny cups.

BUZZARIA approaches SIR BUZZALOT, who stands alone, looking uncomfortable in formal attire.

BUZZARIA
(quiet)
Who organized the funeral?

SIR BUZZALOT
(surprised by the question)
The... the Queen's office. Why?

BUZZARIA
(not answering)
Who paid for it?

SIR BUZZALOT
(thinking)
The Royal Treasury, I assume. Standard for a senior advisor.

BUZZARIA
(nodding, filing the information)
And the flowers?

SIR BUZZALOT
(shrugging)
Donated. By various well-wishers.

BUZZARIA
(skeptical)
Lavender. In winter.

SIR BUZZALOT
(confused)
What does that —

BUZZARIA
(moving away)
Just thinking, Sir Buzzalot. Just thinking.

She approaches the flower arrangement. Lavender. The same lavender from the fields. From the crime scene.

BUZZARIA
(examining the stems)
Freshly cut. Yesterday.
(pause)
Who sent lavender to a funeral in winter?

She plucks a single stem. Tucks it into her coat.

[[marker orange: Lavender at the funeral — who sent it? Follow the paper trail]]


INT. ADMINISTRATIVE FLOOR - DAY [[pink]] #7#

= Buzzaria interviews Pippa Pollen and learns about a forged threatening note.

A bustling office. Workers hurry between desks. The clatter of tiny keyboards and the shuffle of leaf-papers.

PIPPA POLLEN, a nervous young worker bee, sits at a desk covered in pollen logs. Her wings flutter anxiously. She is small, unassuming. The kind of bee you'd overlook.

BUZZARIA
(approaching gently)
Pippa? I'm Detective Buzzaria. I need to ask you a few questions about Mr. Wingsby.

PIPPA
(jumping, startled)
Oh! Detective! I — I didn't see you.
(nervous laughter)
Yes, of course. Whatever you need.

She fidgets with a pollen pen. Her antennae twitch.

BUZZARIA
(sitting across from her, warm)
I understand you worked closely with Mr. Wingsby.

PIPPA
(nodding eagerly)
I was his assistant. For three years. He was... he was a wonderful mentor.
(eyes welling)
He taught me everything about hive administration.

BUZZARIA
(gently)
Did he seem worried about anything lately?

PIPPA
(hesitating)
I... I shouldn't say...

BUZZARIA
(softer)
Pippa. A bee is dead. Anything you tell me could help find his killer.

PIPPA
(after a long pause, whispering)
He said... he said someone was following him. A drone. He didn't say who.
(looking around, lowering her voice further)
And there was a note. On his desk. The morning of...

BUZZARIA
(electrified, but controlled)
What did the note say?

PIPPA
(tearful)
"Your time is running out." That's all. Just those words.
(voice breaking)
I told him to go to security. But he laughed it off. Said it was probably just politics.

BUZZARIA
(urgent)
Where is this note now?

PIPPA
(looking down, ashamed)
I... I threw it away. I was scared.
(pleading)
I didn't think it would lead to this! I thought it was just... office politics!

BUZZARIA
(taking a breath, controlling her frustration)
What did the handwriting look like?

PIPPA
(thinking, trying to remember)
Neat. Very neat. And formal. Not like the usual office scrawl.
(pause, certainty growing)
Like the script from the royal scribe's office. I've seen their work on proclamations.

[[marker orange: Follow up on royal scribe handwriting analysis — CRITICAL LEAD]]

BUZZARIA
(standing, reassuring)
You've been very helpful, Pippa. If you remember anything else, call me.

PIPPA
(nodding, still shaken)
I will. I promise.

Buzzaria leaves. But she pauses outside the door. Pippa's reaction was... interesting.

>IN EVERY CRIME, THERE IS A THOUSAND SMALL CLUES WAITING TO BE FOUND<


INT. DETECTIVE'S OFFICE - LATER [[purple]] #7B#

= Buzzaria analyzes the handwriting forgery and hears from Honeysuckle about pesticide trace on the pollen.

Buzzaria sits at her desk, surrounded by evidence. The lavender stem from the funeral sits in a jar. The pollen sample is under her microscope. The note from Pippa's description is sketched on paper.

She murmurs to herself, thinking out loud.

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
Threatening note. Handwriting like the royal scribe. But Pippa works in the administrative wing...
(tapping a pen)
The royal scribe's office is two floors up. Anyone could have learned to mimic the script.

She pulls out a calligraphy manual from her shelf. Opens it to a page on forgery detection.

BUZZARIA
(reading aloud)
"Handwriting analysis — look for pressure patterns. A forger may copy the shape but not the rhythm."
(studying the sketch)
The pressure here is lighter. Inconsistent with a professional scribe.

She looks at the note from Pippa's description plot. Compares it to a sample of the Queen's handwriting from a proclamation.

BUZZARIA
(noticing a pattern)
The loops are different. The letterforms aren't natural.
(sitting back)
This was forged. And by someone who studied the handwriting — but didn't practice it enough.

She adds this to her evidence board.

[[marker green: Handwriting analysis confirms forgery — killer is NOT royal scribe]]

She picks up her magnifying glass. Examines the lavender stem.

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
The pollen on the victim's wing... lavender.
(holding up the funeral stem)
The flowers at the funeral... lavender.
(pause)
That's not a coincidence.

She looks at her notes from the flower field visitor. She needs to go there.

BUZZARIA
(standing, resolved)
The killer left two calling cards. The pollen at the crime scene. The flowers at the funeral.
(pause)
Same source. Same statement.

Her radio buzzes.

HONEYSUCKLE (V.O.)
Buzz, I finished the pollen analysis. It's from the eastern field. And I found something else...

BUZZARIA
(eager)
What?

HONEYSUCKLE (V.O.)
The pollen sample has a chemical trace. Pesticide.
(beat)
Fresh pesticide. Applied within the last week.

BUZZARIA
(processing)
Someone sprayed the field recently. That means someone was there.
(pause)
Someone who wanted to be there.

She grabs her coat.

BUZZARIA
I'm heading to the eastern field. Send me the coordinates.


INT. SECRET MEETING CHAMBER - NIGHT [[magenta]] #7C#

= Dax Droneworth holds a secret meeting with drones, hinting at a setup for the detective.

A hidden chamber deep in the drone sector. No markings on the entrance. Only a specific knock pattern grants access.

Inside, a dozen drones sit in a circle. DAX DRONEWORTH stands at the center, addressing them.

DAX
(passionate, low voice)
The monarchy has ruled for centuries. And what has it given us?
(pacing)
A queen who governs from above. Workers who serve. Drones who are only useful for mating.
(stopping, scanning faces)
We are more than our biology!

Murmurs of agreement from the assembled drones.

DRONE ONE
(nervous)
But the Queen — she has the guards. The army.

DAX
(confident)
The guards are workers. And the workers are restless.
(leaning in)
Wilfred Wingsby's murder has weakened the throne. The investigation will divide the hive.

DRONE TWO
(doubtful)
What about the detective? She's good. She'll find the truth.

DAX
(smiling thinly)
The truth is whatever we make it.
(beat)
I've made sure there's plenty of evidence pointing away from us.

[[marker red: Dax is manipulating the investigation — plant false leads]]

DRONE THREE
(whispering)
What evidence?

DAX
(mysterious)
Let's just say... the detective will have a very interesting visit to the flower fields.

A buzzer sounds. Warning. Someone is approaching.

DAX
(urgent)
Meeting adjourned. Remember: the future of the hive depends on our discretion.

The drones scatter. The chamber empties in seconds.

!!CLOSE ON A SINGLE COMB — WITH A MONITORING DEVICE

Someone has been watching.

 
INT. ROYAL CHAMBER - NIGHT [[cyan]] #8#

= Buzzaria returns to the scene at night, finding a hidden tunnel leading from the chamber.
 
The hive sleeps. The corridors are silent. Buzzaria returns alone to the crime scene, carrying a tiny ultraviolet lamp.

She approaches the perimeter. The caution tape is still up. The guards are gone — she has pull.

!!EXTREME CLOSE UP: GLOWING POLLEN TRACKS [[shot]]

The chamber is dark, lit only by moonlight filtering through the hive's outer wall. Buzzaria activates her lamp. Ultraviolet light sweeps across the floor.

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
They cleaned the visible evidence. But they missed the invisible.

Lavender pollen tracks glow brightly under UV light. They form a trail — faint, but unmistakable. Leading from the body toward the back wall.

BUZZARIA
(following the trail)
Lavender. The same from the fields.

She reaches the wall. The trail stops. But there should be more...

She examines the comb with her magnifying glass. There! A hairline crack in the wax, forming a perfect rectangle.

BUZZARIA
(pushing gently)
Hidden door.

The comb segment slides open, revealing a dark tunnel. It's narrow — barely wide enough for a bee.

BUZZARIA
(peering inside)
A secondary entrance. Clever.

She pulls out a tiny flashlight. Clicks it on. The light reveals a passage — rough-hewn, not part of the official hive architecture.

BUZZARIA
(realization)
This was dug recently. Someone wanted private access to the royal chamber.

[[marker red: Hidden passage discovered — who built this and why?]]

She enters.


INT. THE HIVE BAR - NIGHT [[orange]] #9# [[storyline Love Affair Subplot]]

= Buzzaria visits the bar, where Beeatrice reveals Wilfred was meeting a royal woman in secret.

THE HONEYPOT — a bustling bar carved into an abandoned honeycomb. Warm amber light. The hum of conversation and the clink of tiny glasses. This is where the hive comes to forget.

!A FIGHT BREAKS OUT at a nearby table.

Two drunk drones tussle over a nectar tab. The barkeeper sighs.

BUZZARIA
(grim)
Some things never change.

The fight is broken up. The drones are escorted out.

BEEATRICE, the bartender, is a world-weary bee with a crooked wing and a gruff exterior. She polishes a glass with a tiny rag, her eyes scanning the room.

BEEATRICE
(without looking at the newcomer)
Buzz. Haven't seen you since the Sticky Situation of last spring.
(she slides a glass across the bar)
Still drinking the usual?

BUZZARIA
(catching the glass with a leg)
You know me too well, Beeatrice.
(taking a sip)
I need information.

BEEATRICE
(raising eyebrow)
You always need information. That's what makes you a good detective.
(leaning on the bar)
And a pain in my thorax.

BUZZARIA
(smiling despite herself)
It's about Wilfred Wingsby.

BEEATRICE
(her expression shifts — too quickly)
What about him?

BUZZARIA
(noticing the shift)
He was a regular here. I have witnesses.

BEEATRICE
(after a pause)
Fine. He was here. Every night for the past two weeks.
(lowering voice)
He'd meet someone. Always in the back booth.
(gesturing with her head)
That one. The dark corner.

BUZZARIA
(intrigued)
Who did he meet?

BEEATRICE
(shrugging)
Couldn't see. They wore a hooded cloak. Happened every night around midnight.
(leaning in)
But I heard her voice.

BUZZARIA
(stunned)
A her?

BEEATRICE
(nodding firmly)
High-pitched. Educated. Like someone from the royal court.
(beat)
Definitely not a worker accent.

BUZZARIA
(processing)
A woman from the royal court. Meeting secretly. Every night.

BEEATRICE
(cryptically)
There's more. The night of the murder — they had a fight. I could hear it from here. Raised voices.
(shaking head)
Then he stormed out. She followed.

[[marker orange: Identify the woman from the royal court — QUEEN?]]

BUZZARIA
(carefully)
Could you identify the voice if you heard it again?

BEEATRICE
(a sly smile)
Maybe. But that depends on what you're willing to trade.

BUZZARIA
(sighing)
Your overdue tab. Consider it paid.

BEEATRICE
(laughing)
That's the Buzz I remember.

!!FOCUS ON THE BACK BOOTH — EMPTY NOW, BUT FULL OF SECRETS



EXT. OLD HIVE SECTION - DAY [[brown]] #10#

= Buzzaria visits Elder Mortis who speaks of the Reformist faction and the true nature of power.

Buzzaria descends to the lower levels. The comb here is older, darker. Fewer bees travel this way. The architecture shifts from geometric perfection to organic chaos.

This is where the oldest bees come to retire. Where memory becomes folklore.

ELDER MORTIS sits on a crumbling comb. He is the oldest living bee in the hive — so ancient his wings are translucent, his eyes clouded with age. But his mind is sharp.

ELDER MORTIS
(raspy, but strong)
I have seen many murders in my time, child.
(pause, counting)
Thirty-seven before the sun set on my youth.
(gesturing)
This one... is different.

BUZZARIA
(sitting beside him, respectfully)
Different how, Elder?

ELDER MORTIS
(tapping his head)
The who is easy. It is always the why that matters.
(turning to face her, his blind eyes piercing)
Why now? Why him? Why in the royal chamber?

BUZZARIA
(pressing)
What can you tell me about power in the hive? The real power?

ELDER MORTIS
(chuckles, a dry rustling sound)
The Queen appears to rule. But it is the advisors who truly govern.
(leaning forward)
The Queen lays eggs. She inspires. But she does not administer.
(tapping his head again)
And when an advisor is murdered, it means the balance is shifting.

BUZZARIA
(urgent)
Shifting how?

ELDER MORTIS
(a long, significant pause)
There is a faction. Drones who believe the monarchy is obsolete.
(whispering)
They call themselves The Reformists.
(pause)
They believe the hive should be a democracy. Every bee gets a vote.

BUZZARIA
(stunned)
That's... that's heresy.

ELDER MORTIS
(enigmatic)
The truth is often called heresy before it becomes law.
(pause)
But not all reformists are idealists.
(significant look)
Some see it as a path to power.

[[marker green: Investigate Reformist faction — Dax Droneworth's connections]]

BUZZARIA
(quiet)
Dax Droneworth?

ELDER MORTIS
(not confirming, not denying)
The head of the serpent is not always its most dangerous part.
(pause)
Look at the body, child. The body of the serpent. The workers who make the movement possible.

>WISDOM COMES WITH AGE, BUT TRUTH COMES WITH PATIENCE<


EXT. FLOWER FIELD - DAY [[green]] #11# [[storyline Pollen Trail]]

= Buzzaria interviews Flora the flower and learns of a limping drone carrying royal comb.

A vast field of lavender stretches to the horizon. The plants sway in the warm breeze. The purple sea is dotted with other bees — workers gathering pollen.

Buzzaria flies low, scanning the ground through her magnifying glass. She lands on a tall lavender stalk.

!!LOW ANGLE THROUGH THE FLOWERS — IMMERSIVE

FLORA, an anthropomorphic flower (as all plants are in this animated world), sways in the breeze. Her petals are a brilliant purple. She has eyes in her center.

FLORA
(cheerful, surprised)
A bee detective! How lovely.
(leaning closer)
We don't get many of your kind out here. Mostly just workers on collection duty.

BUZZARIA
(flattered, but focused)
I need to ask you some questions, ma'am. I'm investigating a murder.

FLORA
(gasping, petals fluttering)
A murder? In our peaceful fields?
(composing herself)
How terrible. Of course, I'll help however I can.

BUZZARIA
The night before last. Did you see anyone come through here? Late?

FLORA
(thinking, her petals tilting)
The night of the storm? Yes! I remember.
(nodding, emphatic)
A bee passed through. Very late. He seemed... nervous.
(acting it out)
Kept looking over his shoulder. Twitching his antennae.

BUZZARIA
(hopeful)
Can you describe him?

FLORA
(trying to remember, closing her eyes)
Large. A drone. Definitely a drone — you can tell by the eyes.
(opening them, certainty growing)
He was carrying something... shiny. A piece of comb. Golden comb.

BUZZARIA
(connecting dots frantically)
Royal comb?

FLORA
(brightening)
Yes! How did you know?
(thinking)
And he had a limp. Favored his left side.

BUZZARIA
(pulling out her notebook, scribbling)
A limp. Left side. Drones don't typically have limps...

FLORA
(helpfully)
Unless they've been injured. Or they're hiding something under their clothes.

Buzzaria freezes.

BUZZARIA
(slowly)
Hiding something.

Disguise. The killer might have been in disguise.

[[marker orange: Check for bees with limps or recent injuries]]


INT. HIVE ARCHIVES - DAY [[brown]] #11B#

= Buzzaria investigates files in the archives and uncovers financial embezzlement from the pollen fund.

The archives are a maze of honeycomb shelves, stretching in every direction. Dust motes float in the amber light. This is where the hive stores its memory — records dating back generations.

ARCHIVIST, a bespectacled, elderly bee with a kindly face, leads Buzzaria through the stacks.

ARCHIVIST
(gesturing proudly)
We have records dating back twelve generations. Every transaction. Every decree. Every marriage.
(humming)
This is the soul of the hive.

BUZZARIA
(focused)
I'm looking for financial records. From the administrative wing. Specifically, the pollen allocation logs from the past three seasons.

ARCHIVIST
(raising an eyebrow)
That's... a lot of reading, Detective.
(pause)
May I ask what this concerns?

BUZZARIA
(quiet)
A murder investigation.

ARCHIVIST
(nodding solemnly)
I see.
(turning)
Follow me.

He leads her to a section labeled POL - BUDGET - 3 SEASONS AGO.

ARCHIVIST
The logs are organized by season. The pollen allocation records will be in the gold binders.

BUZZARIA
(pulling out a binder)
Thank you. This will take a while.

ARCHIVIST
I'll bring you some nectar.

He shuffles off. Buzzaria opens the first binder.

!!MONTAGE — BUZZARIA RESEARCHING

SHOT 1: Buzzaria scans pages of tiny numbers.
SHOT 2: She makes notes in her book.
SHOT 3: She compares two pages side by side.
SHOT 4: Her eyes widen.
SHOT 5: She marks a page.

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
There. Three seasons of discrepancies.
(tracing a column)
Every quarter, a small fraction of the pollen allocation goes missing.
(pause)
Not enough to be noticed. But enough to accumulate.

She does the math in her head. Her expression darkens.

BUZZARIA
(calculating)
Over three years... that's thousands of pollen units. Enough to fund a secret operation.
(beat)
Or to pay for a hidden chamber.

She copies the relevant records. Tucks them into her coat.

BUZZARIA
(standing, determined)
The killer had a financial motive.
(pause)
And I think I know who.

She exits the archives. The Archivist watches her go, a worried expression on his face.

!!CLOSE ON THE ARCHIVES' DOOR — SECRETS KEPT, SECRETS REVEALED




INT. ABANDONED HIVE SECTION - DAY [[grey]] #12#

= Buzzaria meets Larva Lou, who describes a crooked-winged female bee disguised as a drone.

An abandoned section of the hive. Dark. Damp. The buzz of the main hive is distant here. Cracked honeycomb. Dusty corridors. Unused for seasons.

LARVA LOU, a young bee barely out of her cell, emerges from the shadows. She has the restless energy of youth. Her wings are still soft, unfurled only recently.

LARVA LOU
(fidgeting, excited)
You're the detective, right? The one everyone's talking about?

BUZZARIA
(crouching to her level, warm)
That's me. And you are?

LARVA LOU
(proudly)
Lou. I'm Lou. I'm gonna be a detective too, when I grow up!

BUZZARIA
(smiling)
Well, Lou, you can start by telling me if you saw anything unusual the night of the murder.

LARVA LOU
(looking around nervously, then leaning in)
I saw something. The night it happened. I was playing in the back tunnels — I'm not supposed to, but —

BUZZARIA
(reassuring)
You won't get in trouble. I promise. Tell me everything.

LARVA LOU
(taking a deep breath)
I saw two bees. Arguing. Near the vent shaft that leads to the royal level.
(using her hands to demonstrate)
One was Mr. Wingsby. I recognized him from the proclamations.
(her voice drops)
The other... I couldn't see the face. But his shadow...

BUZZARIA
(eager)
What about his shadow?

LARVA LOU
(struggling to articulate)
It looked... wrong. His wing — it was crooked. Not straight like a drone's.
(beat)
And I think I saw... a dress. Under a cloak.

BUZZARIA
(her mind racing)
A dress. So the bee in disguise — was actually a female.

LARVA LOU
(nodding vigorously)
I didn't think of it until now! But yes! It was a girl bee!

[[marker orange: Crooked wing — female bee disguised as a drone]]

>THE TRUTH IS OFTEN HIDDEN IN PLAIN SIGHT — WE JUST NEED TO LOOK<


INT. NEWSROOM - DAY [[blue]] #13#

= Cassandra Comb gives Buzzaria an anonymous tip on royal paper warning about the Queen's lavender meetings.

A chaotic space. Pollen papers fly everywhere. Desks piled high with leaf-notebooks. The clatter of a hundred tiny typewriters fills the air.

CASSANDRA COMB, a sleek, sharp-eyed journalist bee with perfect makeup and a predatory smile, types furiously at her desk. She doesn't look up.

CASSANDRA
(singing it out)
Buzzaria. I was wondering when you'd buzz by. Three murders in five years, and you always visit me after the third interview.

BUZZARIA
(sitting on a spare comb, unfazed)
You heard about the murder.

CASSANDRA
(finally looking up, smug)
Heard? I'm writing about it.
(spinning around in her chair)
"Murder in the Royal Chamber." Exclusive details. Sourced from inside the investigation.

BUZZARIA
(keeping her cool)
Suspiciously fast. Who's your source?

CASSANDRA
(mysterious, enjoying this)
A journalist never reveals her sources, sweetheart. It's in the code.

BUZZARIA
(leaning in, dangerously quiet)
This is a murder investigation, Cassandra. A bee is dead. Someone killed him.
(beat)
If you know something and you're withholding it —

CASSANDRA
(holding up a placating hand)
Relax, Buzz. I'll help.
(reaching into her desk)
I got an anonymous tip. Hand-delivered. On royal paper.

She hands Buzzaria a folded note. The paper is cream-colored, edged with gold.

BUZZARIA
(reading aloud)
"Ask the Queen about the lavender meetings."

CASSANDRA
(smug)
See? I helped.
(winking)
Now put that in your official report and give me an exclusive when you crack it.

BUZZARIA
(folding the note, putting it away)
I'll consider it.

She leaves. But she's thinking. The note confirms Beeatrice's story. And points directly at the Queen.

[[marker purple: Verify handwriting against royal scribe samples]]


INT. HIDDEN CHAMBER - NIGHT [[purple]] #14#

= Buzzaria discovers the secret love nest of Wilfred and the Queen, finding letters and a warning message.

Buzzaria follows the tunnel from the crime scene. It winds deep into the comb. The walls are rough, unfinished.

It opens into a hidden chamber.

BUZZARIA
(breathless)
Oh... wow.

The chamber is luxurious. Furnished with silk tapestries — spider-spun. A bed of soft moss. Scattered lavender petals. Candles made of wax.

This is a love nest.

BUZZARIA
(moving through carefully)
Someone spent a lot of time here.

She finds a scarf — woven from fine spider silk — embroidered with the initials "W.W. + ???"

BUZZARIA
(examining it)
Wilfred Wingsby. And an unknown.

She spots a mirror. On it, written in nectar ink:

"I know."

!!CLOSE ON THE MIRROR — CHILLING

BUZZARIA
(reading)
"I know." Knows what?
(pause)
Knows about the affair? The embezzlement? The conspiracy?

She searches more. Under the moss bed she finds a hidden compartment.

Inside: letters. Dozens of them. Tied with silk thread.

She reads one. Her face changes.

BUZZARIA
(soft, stunned)
These are love letters. From the Queen to Wilfred.

[[marker red: Queen Aster's love letters — motive evidence]]

>THE QUEEN'S SECRET — A LOVE THAT DARED NOT SPEAK ITS NAME<


EXT. HIVE ROOFTOP - NIGHT [[magenta]] #15#

= Buzzaria is attacked by a crooked-winged assailant disguised as a drone on the rooftop.

Buzzaria steps out onto the rooftop. The cool night air revitalizes her. The stars are bright pinpricks against velvet black.

She walks to the edge. Looks out at the hive. Lights glow in thousands of cells.

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
The Queen loved him. The drones hated him. Someone is playing all sides.

Who benefits from the chaos?

A shadow moves behind her. She spins — too late.

A large bee lunges. Their wing is crooked. They grapple. Buzzaria is strong, but the attacker is larger. She's slammed against the comb wall.

ATTACKER
(hissing, voice distorted)
Stop investigating. Or the next sting is yours.

BUZZARIA
(gasping, fighting)
Who... sent you?!

The attacker doesn't answer. They shove her.

!!SLOW MOTION: BUZZARIA FALLS

She tumbles through the air. The ground races toward her.

She spreads her wings. Catches the air. Hovers inches from the ground.

BUZZARIA
(panting, gazing upward)
Crooked wing... female build... disguised as a drone.

She flies back up. The attacker is long gone. But she knows one thing.

BUZZARIA
(determined)
That was our killer. And they're getting desperate.


EXT. HIVE ROOFTOP - CONTINUOUS [[blue]] #15B#

= Buzzaria reflects on her past partner Elias and resolves to continue the work.

Buzzaria doesn't go back inside. She sits on the edge of the roof, looking out at the night sky. Her wings ache from the fall.

She pulls out the photograph from her coat. The one from her desk. Two bees, younger, happier.

FLASHBACK — FIFTEEN SEASONS AGO

A younger BUZZARIA, wings pristine, stands next to a male bee named ELIAS. They are both in uniform — new recruits to the Hive Investigations unit.

ELIAS
(laughing)
Can you believe they gave us badges? We're going to solve every case!

YOUNG BUZZARIA
(bashful)
We haven't even finished training yet.

ELIAS
(nudging her)
Details. I believe in you.

END FLASHBACK

BUZZARIA
(quiet, to the photo)
I got another one, Elias.
(beat)
I solved it.

She touches the photo gently.

BUZZARIA
(softer)
But sometimes I wonder... if you were here... would things be different?

A beat. She puts the photo away.

BUZZARIA
(to herself, resolved)
Doesn't matter. The work continues.

She stands. Spreads her wings. Tests them — they still work.

BUZZARIA
(smiling grimly)
Good enough.

She flies back into the hive.

!!SHOT OF THE HIVE FROM THE ROOFTOP — A CITY OF DREAMS AND SECRETS


INT. NURSERY LEVEL - NIGHT [[pink]] #15C#

= Buzzaria makes a detour to the nursery level, reflecting on the role of bees in the hive.

Before heading to Wilfred's quarters, Buzzaria makes a detour.

The nursery level is quiet at night. Hundreds of larval cells line the walls. Each one contains a developing bee, curled in its cocoon.

A NURSE BEE looks up as Buzzaria enters.

NURSE BEE
(surprised)
Detective? It's late. Is something wrong?

BUZZARIA
(soft)
No. I just... needed to see this.

She walks through the rows. The larvae glow faintly in the dim light.

BUZZARIA
(looking at a cell)
Every bee starts the same.
(pause)
In a cell. Fed royal jelly. Waiting to become who they're meant to be.

NURSE BEE
(gently)
And who are you meant to be, Detective?

BUZZARIA
(a long pause)
Someone who protects the hive.
(turning to the Nurse Bee)
Even from itself.

She watches the larvae for a moment longer. Then she turns and leaves.

The Nurse Bee watches her go, wondering what weighs on the detective's mind.


INT. WILFRED'S QUARTERS - NIGHT [[green]] #16#

= Buzzaria searches Wilfred's quarters and finds a financial ledger pointing to Pippa Pollen's embezzlement.

Wilfred's personal space. It's modest for someone of his rank. Books on economics. A small desk. A single photo of — the Queen.

[[marker green: Note the Queen's photo in his private quarters]]

Buzzaria searches methodically. She opens every drawer. Checks every compartment.

Under the floorboards — a hidden compartment.

Inside: more love letters. But also... a financial ledger.

BUZZARIA
(reading, growing alarmed)
Pollen fund discrepancies. Over three seasons.
(paging through)
Someone has been embezzling from the hive's reserve.

She looks at the numbers more closely. They're complex. But someone has annotated them in the margin.

In Wilfred's handwriting:

"P.P. — confront after the summit."

BUZZARIA
(everything clicking into place)
P.P. Pippa Pollen.

She reads the note again. Her mind reconstructs the scene:

Wilfred discovered the embezzlement. He was going to confront Pippa. Pippa panicked. Pippa killed him.

But... the love letters. The Queen. The hidden chamber. The crooked wing.

BUZZARIA
(sitting back, conflicted)
It all points to Pippa.
(a beat)
But it also points to the Queen.
(another beat)
Someone is framing someone else.

>INVESTIGATION TURNS — THE EVIDENCE POINTS TWO DIRECTIONS AT ONCE<


INT. THRONE ROOM - DUSK [[red]] #17# [[storyline Revelation Sequence]]

= Buzzaria confronts Queen Aster, who admits to the affair but denies the murder.

The sun sets outside. Golden light filters through the western wall. The throne room is empty — the court dismissed.

BUZZARIA stands before QUEEN ASTER. There are no guards. No attendants. Just the two of them.

QUEEN ASTER
(composed, but sad)
I suppose you've found the letters.

BUZZARIA
(slowly)
Yes, Your Majesty. I read them.

QUEEN ASTER
(a long breath)
Wilfred and I were... involved.
(meeting Buzzaria's eyes)
For three years. We kept it hidden.
(pain in her voice)
A queen and her advisor... it would have been a scandal that could split the hive.

BUZZARIA
(careful, quiet)
And the night he died. You met him. In the secret chamber.

QUEEN ASTER
(tears forming, but controlled)
I...
(pause)
Yes. We argued. He wanted to tell the hive. To make our relationship public.
(shaking her head)
I refused. The hive needs stability. A queen's personal life is... complicated.

BUZZARIA
(delicate, probing)
Did you kill him, Your Majesty?

QUEEN ASTER
(instant, firm)
No.
(her voice cracking)
I loved him. I could never...
(collecting herself)
He was the only bee who saw me as more than a monarch.

BUZZARIA
(watching closely)
But you have no alibi for that time.

QUEEN ASTER
(calmly)
No. I was alone. In my chambers. Grieving a decision I had to make.
(beat)
But I understand how it looks.

BUZZARIA
(sighing)
I know who really killed him, Your Majesty. And it wasn't you.

QUEEN ASTER
(surprised)
Who, then?

BUZZARIA
(standing)
I need to confirm one more piece of evidence. But I believe it's Pippa Pollen.

QUEEN ASTER
(shocked)
The secretary? But she's —

BUZZARIA
(nodding)
The one who loved him. In her own way.
(beat)
And the one who embezzled from the hive. Wilfred was going to expose her.

QUEEN ASTER
(slowly understanding)
So she killed him to silence him. And made it look like my doing.

BUZZARIA
(significantly)
She knew about your affair. She used it.




INT. QUEEN'S PRIVATE QUARTERS - NIGHT [[purple]] #17B# [[storyline Character Depth — The Queen's sacrifice]]

= Queen Aster grieves Wilfred and reflects on her royal duty.

After Buzzaria leaves, QUEEN ASTER sits alone in her chambers. The mask of royalty falls away.

She pulls out a hidden compartment in her throne. Inside: a single lavender flower. Pressed. Preserved.

!!FLASHBACK — THREE SEASONS AGO

WILFRED and QUEEN ASTER meet in the hidden chamber. They are younger. Carefree.

WILFRED
(nervous, passionate)
I know this is forbidden. I know the risks.
(taking her leg)
But I cannot pretend anymore.

QUEEN ASTER
(tearful, conflicted)
Wilfred... if the hive finds out...

WILFRED
(gently)
Then we face it together.
(beat)
I love you, Aster. Not the Queen.
(soft)
The bee.

She embraces him. They hold each other in the darkness.

END FLASHBACK

QUEEN ASTER
(holding the flower, whispering)
I'm sorry, Wilfred.
(beat)
I should have said yes. When you asked me to run away.
(pause, tears)
We could have been happy.

She places the flower back. Seals the compartment.

QUEEN ASTER
(to herself)
But I am the Queen. And the hive comes first.
(beat)
Even before love.

She straightens her crown. The monarch returns.



===

# ACT THREE: THE VERDICT

= Buzzaria assembles every piece of evidence. The killer is revealed. Justice is served.


INT. DETECTIVE'S OFFICE - NIGHT [[cyan]] #18#

= Buzzaria maps the evidence, concludes Pippa is the killer, and learns she is trying to flee.

Evidence is pinned to a large board. Strings cross between clues. It looks like a spider's web of investigation.

[[marker orange: Final evidence mapping before confrontation]]

The board shows:

- Lavender pollen - connected to - Flower field / Flora's testimony
- Crooked wing - connected to - Lou's testimony / Rooftop attack
- Royal jelly - connected to - Queen's reserve / Hidden passage
- Love letters - connected to - Queen Aster / Wilfred's quarters
- Hidden chamber - connected to - Secret meetings
- Reformist pamphlet - connected to - Drone uprising / Dax Droneworth
- Embezzlement records - connected to - Pippa Pollen
- Threatening note - connected to - Royal scribe handwriting - Pippa
- Note to Cassandra - connected to - Also royal scribe - Pippa

BUZZARIA
(staring at the board)
There it is. The shape of the truth.

She traces the strings. Every path leads to one name:

PIPPA POLLEN.

BUZZARIA
(rehearsing her case)
She had motive: embezzlement exposure.
(she touches another string)
She had means: access to the royal chamber via the hidden passage.
(she touches another)
She had knowledge: of the Queen's affair, to craft her frame.

Her communicator buzzes. She answers.

SIR BUZZALOT (V.O.)
Detective! We have a situation at the transport tunnels. Pippa Pollen is attempting to flee the hive!

BUZZARIA
(grabbing her coat)
Seal all exits. I'm on my way.

>A DETECTIVE'S WORK IS NEVER DONE — ESPECIALLY NOT AT THE END<


INT. GRAND HALL - NIGHT [[orange]] #19#

= Buzzaria gathers the suspects in the grand hall and begins her summation.

The grand hall is packed. Thousands of bees fill the space — on the walls, the ceiling, the floor. The hum of a thousand wings creates a constant drone.

At the center: a semicircle of suspects.

DAX DRONEWORTH stands with his arms crossed. QUEEN ASTER sits on a portable throne. SIR BUZZALOT stands at attention. HONEYSUCKLE takes notes. DR. STINGSON cleans his glasses. CASSANDRA COMB watches with a reporter's hunger.

And PIPPA POLLEN stands to one side, looking terrified.

BUZZARIA enters. The crowd partes for her. She walks to the center.

BUZZARIA
(projecting, commanding)
I have gathered you here to reveal the identity of Wilfred Wingsby's murderer.

Murmurs ripple through the crowd. Wings buzz with anticipation.

BUZZARIA
(BEGINNING her summation, pacing)
The crime scene told me several things.
(holding up a leg)
First: the sting was precise. Professional. Not a crime of passion.
(second leg)
Second: the lavender pollen on the victim's wing led me to the eastern fields.
(third leg)
And third: the royal jelly fragment in the wound was a plant. Meant to frame the Queen.

She walks slowly, deliberately. Every eye follows her.

DAX
(interrupting, irritated)
This is all fascinating, Detective, but some of us have a hive to run.

BUZZARIA
(turning to him, sharp)
You have an alibi, Dax. A solid one. Dozens of witnesses placing you in a budget meeting.

DAX
(smug, smiling)
That's right. So I'm clear.

BUZZARIA
(nodding)
Yes. You are.
(beat, turning away)
Which is why you didn't do it.

The crowd gasps. Dax's smile freezes.

The crowd ERUPTS in chaotic conversation. Bees shout over each other.

!!CACOPHONY OF VOICES

SIR BUZZALOT
(above the noise)
Order! ORDER!

He slams his staff against the comb floor. The sound reverberates.

The crowd settles. But the tension remains.

QUEEN ASTER
(calmly, commanding)
Let her speak.

All eyes turn to Buzzaria.


INT. GRAND HALL - CONTINUOUS [[red]] #20#

= Buzzaria exposes Pippa Pollen as the killer, who breaks down and confesses.

The tension is electric. Buzzaria faces the semicircle.

BUZZARIA
(voice building)
The murder was committed by someone with access to the royal chamber.
(gesturing)
Someone who knew about the hidden passage — because they dug it themselves.
(another gesture)
Someone who could forge the Queen's handwriting — because they studied it.
(pause)
Someone who loved Wilfred Wingsby. And someone he was about to destroy.

A beat. The crowd waits.

The room splits into two reactions:

HONEYSUCKLE
(to Dr. Stingson, analyzing in real time)
The physics of the passage match a smaller build. A worker. Not a drone.

DR. STINGSON
(nodding, professional)
Consistent with the wound angle. Smaller assailant.

DR. STINGSON ^
(tapping notes)
The toxin confirms bee venom.

HONEYSUCKLE ^
(marking her board)
And the pollen trail matches the administrative wing.

They realize they're speaking together. They stop.

HONEYSUCKLE
(a wry smile)
Great minds.

DR. STINGSON
(returning it)
Indeed.

She walks slowly toward PIPPA POLLEN.

PIPPA
(nervous laughter)
Me? I'm just a secretary! I don't — I can't — this is insane!

BUZZARIA
(calm, relentless)
You studied calligraphy at the Royal Academy. Your handwriting is identical to the royal scribe's.
(holding up evidence)
The love letters from the hidden chamber? You wrote them. Not the Queen.
(another piece)
The threatening note on his desk? You left it.
(another)
The tip to Cassandra? You sent it.

PIPPA
(backing away, shaking)
No! I would never — !

BUZZARIA
(inexorable)
The night of the murder, you followed Wilfred through the hidden passage. You wore a disguise — padding to look like a drone, a fake crooked wing to throw off suspicion.
(pressing)
You argued. He had discovered the embezzlement. Three seasons of stolen pollen.

PIPPA
(voice cracking)
He was... he was going to fire me. Ruin me.
(tears streaming)
I just needed more time to pay it back! I was going to return everything!

BUZZARIA
(quiet, but steel)
So you stung him. Twice. The first time — you hesitated. The second — you finished the job.

PIPPA
(sobbing now, collapsing)
I loved him!
(looking up, desperate)
I thought... if he saw me... if the Queen was blamed... he would finally notice me!

BUZZARIA
(gently, but sad)
Love doesn't give you the right to take a life, Pippa.

>THE KILLER IS REVEALED — A HEART BROKEN INTO BETRAYAL < AND MURDER<


INT. HIVE EXIT TUNNEL - CONTINUOUS [[magenta]] #21#

= Pippa flees but is cornered and apprehended by Buzzaria and the guards.

PIPPA bolts.

She is fast. She weaves through the crowd. Bees scatter.

BUZZARIA
(giving chase)
Stop her! Seal the exits!

!!ACTION SEQUENCE — CHAOS IN THE HIVE

Pippa rips off her disguise. Her real wings are revealed — they are crooked naturally. The padding was to hide them, not fake them.

She spirals through the hive. Buzzaria follows. They dodge hanging comb. Weave through worker traffic.

PIPPA
(screaming, hysterical)
You don't understand! He made me feel invisible!
(sobbing as she flies)
Every day! For three years! And he never saw me!

BUZZARIA
(struggling to keep up, calling out)
Murder is never the answer, Pippa! Never!

Pippa reaches the transport tunnel. It leads outside. A gust of wind almost sweeps her off course.

SIR BUZZALOT and guards emerge from a side passage. They block her path.

She's cornered.

PIPPA
(defeated, sinking to the floor)
I just wanted to be seen.
(quiet, broken)
I just wanted him to love me.

BUZZARIA
(landing nearby, exhausted)
I know.
(pause)
But this wasn't the way.

The guards move in. They gently take Pippa into custody. She doesn't resist.

PIPPA
(looking back at Buzzaria, broken)
Will you tell him? When you see him?
(quiet)
Tell him I'm sorry.

BUZZARIA
(soft)
I will.

Pippa is led away. Buzzaria watches them go.

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
Another life destroyed by secrets.

SIR BUZZALOT approaches. He looks shaken.

SIR BUZZALOT
(quiet)
I... I can't believe it was her. She was always so quiet.

BUZZARIA
(sighing)
The quiet ones are the ones who break the hardest.

SIR BUZZALOT
(confused)
What do you mean?

BUZZARIA
(turning to him)
Pippa spent three years invisible. Working beside a bee she loved, who never saw her.
(beat)
That kind of silence... eventually it explodes.

SIR BUZZALOT
(sobering)
Will she stand trial?

BUZZARIA
Yes. The council will decide her fate.
(pause, looking at the sky)
But I think... there's room for mercy here.

SIR BUZZALOT
(surprised)
Mercy? She killed someone.

BUZZARIA
(grim)
She killed someone because the system failed her. Because she had no voice.
(beat)
That doesn't excuse the act. But it explains it.

SIR BUZZALOT
(a long pause)
You're wiser than you let on, Buzz.

BUZZARIA
(small, tired smile)
Don't tell anyone.


INT. COUNCIL CHAMBER - DAY [[purple]] #21B# [[storyline Justice and Mercy — The Queen's compassion]]

= Pippa stands trial and Queen Aster sentences her to labor in the pollen fields.

An official proceeding. The council — twelve elder bees — sits in a semicircle. PIPPA POLLEN stands before them, shackled.

QUEEN ASTER presides from a raised throne.

COUNCIL ELDER
(reading the charges)
Pippa Pollen, you are charged with the murder of Wilfred Wingsby. How do you plead?

PIPPA
(head bowed, whispering)
Guilty.

Murmurs through the chamber. The crowd stirs.

QUEEN ASTER
(raising a wing for silence)
Before we pass judgment, I would like to speak.

She stands. Walks down to Pippa's level.

QUEEN ASTER
(softly, for all to hear)
I have spent my entire life alone. Surrounded by thousands, but known by none.
(looking at Pippa)
I understand the desperation of wanting to be seen.

PIPPA
(looking up, tearful)
Your Majesty...

QUEEN ASTER
(continuing)
But the path you chose was wrong. Violence is never the answer.
(pause)
However...

She turns to the council.

QUEEN ASTER
...this court acknowledges the circumstances that led to this tragedy.
(firm)
Pippa Pollen, you are sentenced to ten seasons of service in the pollen fields. You will repay the embezzled funds. And when your sentence is complete, you will be reintegrated into the hive.

Gasps from the crowd. The punishment is lenient.

COUNCIL ELDER
(objecting)
Your Majesty! This is murder! The standard sentence is —

@A VOICE FROM THE CROWD
(anonymous)
She deserves death!

QUEEN ASTER
(cutting him off, steel)
The standard sentence is what I say it is.
(softer)
This hive has lost enough to violence. We will not add to it.

PIPPA
(breaking down)
Thank you, Your Majesty. I... I will serve my sentence. And I will repent.

The guards lead her away. The crowd buzzes with conversation.

QUEEN ASTER meets BUZZARIA's eyes across the room. A moment of mutual understanding.




EXT. OPEN FIELD - DAWN [[green]] #22#

= Queen Aster and Buzzaria watch the sunrise and discuss real reforms for the workers.

The sun rises over the meadow. Golden light spills across the flowers. The hive stirs to life.

Pippa is taken away by transport guards. Buzzaria watches from the hive entrance. She looks tired. Old.

QUEEN ASTER approaches. She looks smaller than she did in the throne room.

QUEEN ASTER
(a long silence)
Thank you, Detective. For the truth.

BUZZARIA
(not looking at her, quiet)
The truth doesn't bring him back.

QUEEN ASTER
No.
(pause)
But it heals the hive.
(beat)
I have spoken to the council. We will announce reforms. Real reforms.
(she turns to face Buzzaria)
Workers will have representation. The drone caucus will be restructured.
(softer)
Pippa's story is not just hers. It's the story of every worker who felt invisible.

BUZZARIA
(finaly looking at her, earnest)
That's a good start, Your Majesty.

QUEEN ASTER
(small, sad smile)
It's what Wilfred would have wanted.

They watch the sunrise together. A golden bloom across the meadow.

!!WIDE SHOT OF THE HIVE AT DAWN — HOPE RENEWED

[[marker green: Story resolution — justice served, hive moving forward]]


INT. THE HIVE BAR - DAY [[blue]] #23# [[storyline Epilogue]]

= Buzzaria and Beeatrice share a drink, reflecting on the systemic failures behind the crime.

The Honeypot is quiet. The lunch rush hasn't started. Beeatrice polishes glasses behind the bar.

BUZZARIA sits at the counter. A glass of well-earned nectar in front of her.

BEEATRICE
(breaking the silence)
So. Another case closed, eh?

BUZZARIA
(sipping her nectar)
Another case.
(thoughtful)
The sting of truth, as they say.

BEEATRICE
(laughing, shaking her head)
You're getting soft, Buzz. I remember a time you'd be celebrating right now.

BUZZARIA
(small, rueful smile)
Maybe I'm just tired.
(pause)
Or maybe I'm starting to wonder...

BEEATRICE
(prompting)
Wonder what?

BUZZARIA
(putting down her glass)
We catch the one who did the deed. But what about the system that made them feel like they had no other choice?
(beat)
What about the invisibility? The desperation?

BEEATRICE
(leaning on the bar, serious)
That's above our pay grade, Buzz.

BUZZARIA
(a long sigh)
Yeah. I know.
(raising her glass)
But someone has to think about it.

BEEATRICE
(clinking her glass with Buzzaria's)
Then I'm glad it's you.

They drink. Two old friends, sharing a moment of quiet understanding.




EXT. FLOWER FIELD - SUNSET [[orange]] #24#

= Buzzaria returns to the lavender fields to speak with Flora and find some peace.

Buzzaria returns to the lavender field. The colors are golden in the setting sun. FLORA sways gently.

FLORA
(gently, wise)
You solved it, didn't you?

BUZZARIA
(sitting on a lavender stalk)
Yes. But it doesn't feel like a win.

FLORA
(nodding, her petals rustling)
The best truths never do.
(beat)
They're heavy. Like nectar that hasn't been processed yet.
(thoughtful)
But they must be carried. Because they're real.

BUZZARIA
(touching a lavender petal gently)
I'll carry it.

FLORA
(sagely)
The flower that bends in the wind survives the storm.
(softly)
You are that flower, Detective.

They watch the sun dip below the horizon. Birds fly in the distance. The world buzzes on.

BUZZARIA
(quiet, resolved)
Another day. Another case.
(pause)
But maybe... a better world tomorrow.

She spreads her wings. Takes off. Hovers for a moment.

BUZZARIA
(calling back to Flora)
Thank you. For the wisdom.

FLORA
(smiling with her petals)
Come back anytime, Detective. The flowers always bloom for those who seek the truth.

Buzzaria flies toward the hive. The lights of the great city twinkle in the growing dark.

>A DETECTIVE'S WORK IS NEVER DONE — BUT SOMETIMES, THERE IS PEACE<


INT. DETECTIVE'S OFFICE - MORNING [[blue]] #25#

= Buzzaria files the case, stores the recording, and is summoned to the council.

Three days later.

Buzzaria sits at her desk. The evidence board has been taken down. The case files are filed.

She holds the recording device from the hidden chamber. The last piece of evidence.

She presses play one more time.

RECORDING (PIPPA'S VOICE)
(soft, on the recording)
I'm sorry, Wilfred. I'm sorry for everything.

BUZZARIA
(stopping the recording, quiet)
So am I.

She places the device in a labeled evidence bag. Seals it.

The phone buzzes. She picks up.

BUZZARIA
(into phone)
Detective Honeydew.
(pause, slight surprise)
Council chambers? Now?
(pause)
I'll be right there.

She hangs up. Stands. Straightens her badge.

BUZZARIA
(to herself)
The work continues.

She exits. The office is empty.

!!PUSH IN ON THE PHOTO OF ELIAS — A REMINDER OF WHAT MATTERS


INT. COUNCIL CHAMBER - DAY [[gold]]

= Buzzaria is awarded the Hive's Highest Honor, the Golden Sting.

BUZZARIA enters the council chamber. The elders are assembled. QUEEN ASTER sits at the head.

QUEEN ASTER
(solemn)
Detective. Thank you for coming.

BUZZARIA
(alert)
What's this about, Your Majesty?

QUEEN ASTER
(standing)
The council has reviewed your service record. Twenty seasons of dedicated investigation.
(pause)
We have decided to award you the Hive's Highest Honor — the Golden Sting.

BUZZARIA
(taken aback)
Your Majesty, I — that's unnecessary.

QUEEN ASTER
(firm)
It is necessary. The hive must honor those who seek the truth.
(small smile)
And you, Detective, have stung the truth more times than any bee in history.

She presents a small, golden badge — a sting made of pure honey-gold.

BUZZARIA
(taking it, humbled)
Thank you, Your Majesty.

QUEEN ASTER
(softly)
Thank you, Buzzaria.

A round of applause from the council.

[[marker green: Buzzaria receives the Golden Sting — recognition for her service]]


INT. THE HIVE BAR - NIGHT [[orange]] #27#

= The hive celebrates Buzzaria's success at the bar with Beeatrice.

Later that night. The Honeypot is celebrating.

Bees raise their glasses. Beeatrice pours round after round.

BEEATRICE
(shouting over the noise)
To Buzz! The best detective in the hive!

Cheers. Glasses clink.

BUZZARIA
(flustered, embarrassed)
I didn't ask for this.

BEEATRICE
(grinning)
Too bad! You're getting it!

She slides Buzzaria a special drink — a golden nectar, shimmering.

BEEATRICE
On the house.

BUZZARIA
(taking it, smiling)
Thanks, Beeatrice.

BEEATRICE
(a rare sincere moment)
You earned it, Buzz.
(beat)
The hive is better because of you.

BUZZARIA
(a long, grateful look)
I couldn't have done it without you.

BEEATRICE
(waving dismissively)
I just poured drinks.

BUZZARIA
(sipping)
You poured more than that. You poured truth.

They share a look. Two old friends, understanding each other.

!!WIDE ON THE BAR — A HIVE CELEBRATING ITS DETECTIVE


INT. DETECTIVE'S OFFICE - LATER THAT NIGHT [[purple]] #28#

= Buzzaria pins her new badge next to Elias's photo and turns off the light.

The party faded. Buzzaria returns to her office. Alone.

She pins the Golden Sting badge next to Elias's photo.

BUZZARIA
(looking at the photo)
See, Elias? I made good.
(beat)
I hope you're proud.

She turns off the light. The office falls into darkness.

But outside, the hive glows. Alive. Vibrant. Healing.

!!WIDE SHOT OF THE HIVE AT NIGHT — A CIVILIZATION ENDURES

>FOR EVERY ENDING, THERE IS A NEW BEGINNING<


# FINAL NOTE

= This story is dedicated to every creature who searches for truth in a world of secrets.

THE END

>THE STING OF TRUTH — A BUZZARIA HONEYDEW MYSTERY<


~~~

~Buzz buzz buzz, the hive still hums~
~Under the light of a thousand suns~
~Secrets buried in honey and wax~
~The truth will find its way back~

~Wings that carry heavy loads~
~Travel down the winding roads~
~Every sting and every tear~
~Brings the honest heart to fear~

~But in the darkness of the comb~
~The detective finds her home~
~Seeking truth in every cell~
~Breaking the conspirator's spell~

~Buzz buzz buzz, the story's told~
~Of love and loss and courage bold~
~The hive will heal, the wounds will mend~
~The mystery finds its final end~

